Every token in pequod-variables.scss (light) / pequod-variables-dark.scss (dark) is declared with !default, so any earlier declaration with the same name wins. Drop a tiny SCSS overrides file into your project and prepend it to the theme list:
// my-overrides.scss
/*-- scss:defaults --*/

// Crank Starbuck's link colour darker for a print-leaning publication.
$starbuck: #00658E !default;

// Or shift the log-50 paper towards a colder white.
$log-50: #F5F2EC !default;
Wire it in:
format:
  pequod-revealjs:
    theme:
      - my-overrides.scss
      - default
The default line keeps Quarto’s default theme participating; the extension’s own SCSS is added by Quarto automatically.

