Focus indicator
:focus-visible carries a body-colour outline + a Starbuck box-shadow glow.
:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid $body-color;
  outline-offset: 2px;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px rgba($link-color, 0.35);
}
A pure-blue outline alone would not pass WCAG 1.4.11 contrast against the warm-paper background (~3:1, below the 3:1 cap-floor for non-text contrast against an adjacent colour). The body-colour outline carries the primary contrast; the Starbuck glow rides as the brand cue.

Read the active set from JS
const root = document.documentElement;
const series = Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) =&gt;
  getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(`--pequod-chart-${i + 1}`).trim()
);
The values flip automatically when the user toggles light / dark because the dark stylesheet redeclares the same custom properties under its own :root. Charts that pull from getComputedStyle at each render pick the new palette up without rerunning the layout pipeline.

Read from an Observable cell
// Pull all eight slots into an array Observable can use as a scale.
const pequod = Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) =&gt;
  getComputedStyle(document.documentElement)
    .getPropertyValue(`--pequod-chart-${i + 1}`)
    .trim()
);

Plot.plot({
  marks: [
    Plot.barY(data, { x: "category", y: "value", fill: "category" })
  ],
  color: { range: pequod }
})
